Your password has been changed.

It is shorter than $_arg_limit characters.  That is accepted, but worth
telling you about: NIST SP 800-63B asks for at least that many for a
password that is used on its own, and an fml administrator password is
used on its own.

  https://pages.nist.gov/800-63-4/sp800-63b.html

There is no requirement to mix letters, digits and symbols.  Length is
what is being asked for, so a longer phrase you can remember serves
better than a short one made awkward.
